<title>UK: Hardy Oil takes East Midlands' FTSE spot.</title>
<headline>Hardy Oil takes East Midlands' FTSE spot.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The UK's East Midlands Electricity will be replaced in the FTSE 250 index by energy company Hardy Oil &amp; Gas Plc after the regional electricity company's takeover by Dominion Resources was declared unconditional last week.</p>
<p>The FTSE Actuaries said that Hardy would also become a member of the FTSE 350 Lower Yield Index and would be removed from the FTSE SmallCap Index.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4020</p>
</text>
